chezmoi dots secrets run — Run a declared CLI with its access token injected

USAGE
  chezmoi dots secrets run <name> [--timeout <duration>] [--] [<args>...]

ARGUMENTS
  name  Secret declared in .chezmoidata/secrets.toml. Only kind bws has a token to inject; bw and rbw use their own session (BW_SESSION, the rbw agent) and exit 2.
  --  Everything after the first -- goes to the CLI verbatim and is never parsed here, so its own flags (-h, --output) pass through; put the CLI's arguments after it.
  The token comes from the keyring entry the registry names and goes only into the CLI's environment (BWS_ACCESS_TOKEN), never its arguments. The CLI is the entry's command or the kind's name on PATH, run without a shell. What the CLI prints is not filtered.
  Exit codes: the CLI's own exit code; 2 for a usage error or a name that is not declared; 1 for a missing CLI or token, an invalid registry or a timeout.

OPTIONS
  -h, --help  Show this help and exit successfully.
  --timeout <duration>  stop the CLI after this duration (0 means no timeout) (default: "0s")

ENVIRONMENT
  CHEZMOI_EXECUTABLE  chezmoi executable (default: chezmoi).
  CHEZMOI_CONFIG_FILE  chezmoi config file (default: chezmoi's config).
  CHEZMOI_SOURCE_DIR  source directory (default: ask chezmoi; honors .chezmoiroot).

EXAMPLES
  chezmoi dots secrets run example-vault -- secret list 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000 --output json --color no
  chezmoi dots secrets run example-vault -- project list
